Every word a download notification can show — screen SCR-802.

Committed here rather than added to `taffy_android_strings.grd`, following
`../../../java/res/values/taffy_assistant_island_strings.xml`: a committed
resource directory is where a package is pinned, and it is what produces the
`R.string` a Kotlin or Java source can name. The grd's messages are the pak
half, read by browser-process C++, and the two never carry the same message
twice — a string with two homes is a string that will one day disagree with
itself.

Four states and three controls, and the set is closed. A download is not a task:
it has no sources and no partial result, so none of the assistant's seven
states appears here.
-->
<resources>
  <string name="taffy_download_channel_name">Downloads</string>
  <string name="taffy_download_channel_description">Progress and results for files you download.</string>
  <string name="taffy_download_hidden">Download update</string>
  <string name="taffy_download_share">Share download</string>

  <string name="taffy_download_running">Downloading %1$s</string>
  <string name="taffy_download_paused">Paused %1$s</string>
  <string name="taffy_download_complete">Downloaded %1$s</string>
  <!-- Not "Download failed": the catalog's copy rules ask for the actor and a
       plain verb, and a person reads this to find out what to do next. -->
  <string name="taffy_download_failed">Couldn\'t download %1$s</string>

  <string name="taffy_download_pause">Pause</string>
  <string name="taffy_download_resume">Resume</string>
  <string name="taffy_download_cancel">Cancel</string>
</resources>
